<style>
:root {
  --bg: #0A0A0B;
  --surface: #14141A;
  --panel: #1A1A22;
  --ink-1: #F5F5EE;
  --ink-2: #A0A09A;
  --ink-3: #5C5C58;
  --rule: #26262C;
  --yellow: #FFE600;
  --crimson: #E84B5F;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink-1); }
body {
  font-family: 'Inter Tight', system-ui, sans-serif;
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.65;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  font-feature-settings: "ss01" on, "cv11" on;
}
.wrap { max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 64px 24px 96px; }

.eyebrow {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.2em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-3);
  margin-bottom: 16px;
}
.eyebrow .dash { color: var(--yellow); margin: 0 10px; }

h1.title {
  font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: clamp(36px, 5.6vw, 60px);
  line-height: 1.02;
  letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  margin: 0 0 22px;
  color: var(--ink-1);
  font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 50, "WONK" 0;
}
h1 em {
  font-style: italic;
  font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 100, "WONK" 1;
  color: var(--yellow);
  font-weight: 400;
}

.standfirst {
  font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  font-weight: 400;
  font-size: clamp(19px, 1.6vw, 22px);
  line-height: 1.45;
  color: var(--ink-2);
  max-width: 760px;
  margin: 0 0 56px;
  font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 100, "opsz" 32;
}

.takeaways {
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  padding: 32px 36px;
  margin: 0 0 56px;
}
.takeaways h2 {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.2em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--yellow);
  margin: 0 0 22px;
  font-weight: 500;
}
.takeaways ol {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(380px, 1fr));
  gap: 0;
}
.takeaways li {
  padding: 18px 24px 18px 20px;
  border-left: 2px solid var(--yellow);
  margin: 0 0 4px;
  background: transparent;
  font-size: 15.5px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  color: var(--ink-1);
}
.takeaways li .n {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  color: var(--yellow);
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 4px;
  font-weight: 500;
}
.takeaways li strong { color: var(--ink-1); font-weight: 600; }

.byline {
  display: flex; gap: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap;
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--ink-3);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  padding: 16px 0;
  margin-bottom: 44px;
}
.byline strong { color: var(--ink-1); font-weight: 500; }

.stats-row {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  gap: 0;
  margin: 0 0 44px;
  border-top: 2px solid var(--ink-1);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
}
.stat {
  padding: 20px 24px 20px 0;
  border-right: 1px solid var(--rule);
}
.stat:last-child { border-right: none; }
.stat .num {
  font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: 46px;
  line-height: 1;
  letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  display: block;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  color: var(--ink-1);
}
.stat .num .unit { font-size: 16px; color: var(--ink-3); font-weight: 400; margin-left: 4px; }
.stat .lbl {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 10px;
  letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-3);
  margin-top: 10px;
  display: block;
}
.stat.accent .num { color: var(--yellow); }

section { margin-bottom: 56px; }
.chart-frame {
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  padding: 36px 32px 28px;
  margin: 0 0 16px;
  position: relative;
}
.chart-frame h2 {
  font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: 28px;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  margin: 0 0 6px;
  color: var(--ink-1);
  font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 60;
}
.chart-frame .sub {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  color: var(--ink-3);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  margin-bottom: 24px;
}
.chart-frame p.lede {
  color: var(--ink-2);
  margin: 0 0 28px;
  max-width: 760px;
  font-size: 16px;
}
svg.hyrox-chart { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }

.faq {
  margin: 56px auto;
  max-width: 880px;
}
.faq h2 {
  font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: 36px;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  margin: 0 0 28px;
  color: var(--ink-1);
}
.faq details {
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  padding: 22px 4px;
}
.faq details:first-of-type { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.faq details summary {
  cursor: pointer;
  font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: 20px;
  color: var(--ink-1);
  list-style: none;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 20px;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
}
.faq details summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
.faq details summary::after {
  content: '+';
  font-family: 'Inter Tight', sans-serif;
  font-weight: 300;
  font-size: 28px;
  color: var(--yellow);
  transition: transform 0.2s;
  line-height: 1;
}
.faq details[open] summary::after { content: '−'; }
.faq details p {
  margin: 16px 0 4px;
  color: var(--ink-2);
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 1.7;
}

.method {
  margin-top: 60px;
  padding: 28px 32px;
  background: var(--surface);
  border-left: 3px solid var(--yellow);
  font-size: 14.5px;
  color: var(--ink-2);
  max-width: 880px;
}
.method h3 {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  margin: 0 0 12px;
  color: var(--ink-1);
  font-weight: 500;
}
.method p { margin: 0 0 10px; }
.method p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

@media (max-width: 720px) {
  .wrap { padding: 44px 18px 64px; }
  .stats-row { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  .stat { padding: 16px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .stat:nth-child(2) { border-right: none; }
  .stat:nth-child(3), .stat:nth-child(4) { border-bottom: none; }
  .chart-frame { padding: 24px 16px 16px; }
  .takeaways { padding: 24px 20px; }
  .takeaways ol { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <div class="eyebrow">HYROX <span class="dash">/</span> Bengaluru 2026 <span class="dash">/</span> Calorie Analysis</div>

  <h1 class="title">How many <em>calories</em> does HYROX burn?</h1>

  <p class="standfirst">
    1,441 kilocalories across 2 hours and 1 minute of HYROX, ranked segment by
    segment. The longest two stations cost more than the highest-HR ones — duration
    beats intensity for total burn.
  </p>

  <div class="takeaways">
    <h2>Key takeaways</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <span class="n">01 — TOTAL</span>
        <strong>A 2:01:06 HYROX burned 1,441 kcal.</strong> That's about 11.9 kcal per minute across
        the full race window — comparable to sustaining a hard tempo run for two hours straight.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">02 — TOPS THE LIST</span>
        <strong>Wall Balls and Sled Pull tied at 115 kcal each — the costliest segments of the race.</strong>
        Both are also the two longest segments (11:28 and 10:01). Time on the floor wins.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">03 — DURATION &gt; INTENSITY</span>
        <strong>The five most expensive segments are also the five longest.</strong> Per-minute differences
        in intensity are smaller than per-segment differences in duration. To raise total burn, lengthen
        what you do; you don't have to suffer harder.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">04 — RUNS ≈ STATIONS</span>
        <strong>Running segments collectively burned 691 kcal; stations burned 632 kcal.</strong>
        Roxzone transitions added another 118 kcal. The metabolic split is roughly 48% running, 44%
        stations, 8% transitions — HYROX is genuinely a hybrid race by energy cost.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">05 — CHEAPEST</span>
        <strong>Farmers Carry burned just 29 kcal — by far the cheapest segment.</strong> At 2:29 it's
        also the shortest. Per-minute burn rate was actually competitive with the heavy stations;
        the total is small because the segment is brief, not because the effort is easy.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="byline">
    <div>By <strong>Prashant Singh</strong></div>
    <div>Bib <strong>95039</strong></div>
    <div>Age group <strong>30–34</strong></div>
    <div>Race <strong>12 April 2026</strong></div>
    <div>Final time <strong>02:01:06</strong></div>
    <div>Tracker <strong>Apple Watch</strong></div>
  </div>

  <div class="stats-row">
    <div class="stat accent">
      <span class="num">1,441<span class="unit">kcal</span></span>
      <span class="lbl">Total energy burned</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <span class="num">11.9<span class="unit">kcal/min</span></span>
      <span class="lbl">Average burn rate</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <span class="num">115<span class="unit">kcal</span></span>
      <span class="lbl">Costliest segment</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <span class="num">2:01:06</span>
      <span class="lbl">Total race time</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="chart-frame">
      <h2>Every segment, ranked by cost</h2>
      <div class="sub">Active energy per segment · sorted highest to lowest · yellow = station, grey = run</div>
      <p class="lede">
        Stations cluster at the top of the list because they're long. Runs spread through the middle.
        The shortest segment, Farmers Carry, sits at the bottom — not because it was easy but because
        2 minutes 29 seconds wasn't long enough to accumulate.
      </p>
      <CaloriesPerStation raceData={raceData} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>How many calories does a HYROX race burn?</summary>
      <p>For this 2:01:06 race, the Apple Watch recorded 1,441 kcal of active energy across all 16 segments — an average of about 11.9 kcal per minute. That's comparable to a sustained hard tempo run kept up for two hours. Individual burn varies with body weight, finishing time, and effort. A faster 90-minute finish on the same body would burn less because total time-on-floor is shorter; a slower 2:30 finish would burn more.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Which HYROX station burns the most calories?</summary>
      <p>In this race, Wall Balls and Sled Pull tied as the costliest segments at 115 kcal each. They're also the two longest segments in the race — Wall Balls at 11:28 and Sled Pull at 10:01. The pattern holds across the data: duration drives total cost more than intensity does. Sled Pull is particularly notable because it had the lowest average heart rate of any station (158 bpm) yet topped the calorie chart — the long, technical, stop-start nature kept HR moderate but total time-under-load high.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do HYROX runs or stations burn more calories?</summary>
      <p>Approximately equal. In this race, the eight running segments collectively burned 691 kcal and the eight workout stations burned 632 kcal. Roxzone transitions accounted for the remaining ~118 kcal. The metabolic split was roughly 48% running, 44% stations, and 8% transitions. HYROX is genuinely a hybrid race by energy cost, not a "running race with some stations attached."</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How was this calorie data measured?</summary>
      <p>Active energy was captured on an Apple Watch during a Mixed Cardio workout session and exported as JSON via the Health Auto Export iOS app. Apple's <code>active_energy</code> metric estimates expenditure above resting metabolic rate, computed from heart rate and motion data. It's an estimate, not a metabolic-cart measurement — absolute values can vary between athletes by 10–15% — but the metric is internally consistent within a single athlete's data, which makes it useful for comparing segments within one race.</p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <div class="method">
    <h3>Methodology &amp; data provenance</h3>
    <p>
      Active energy was captured on an Apple Watch during a Mixed Cardio workout
      (started 09:50:10 IST, ended 11:51:38 IST on 12 April 2026), exported via the
      Health Auto Export iOS app as JSON. Apple's <code>active_energy</code> metric
      estimates expenditure above resting metabolic rate, computed from heart rate
      and motion sensors. The Watch reports values in kilojoules; figures here are
      converted to kilocalories at 1 kcal = 4.184 kJ.
    </p>
    <p>
      Per-segment totals are computed by summing active_energy samples that fall
      within each segment's start and end time, using durations taken from the
      official HYROX race results (bib 95039, HYROX Bengaluru 2026, Sunday division).
      The 10:12 of total roxzone time is distributed equally as ~41 seconds between
      each of the 15 segment transitions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Apple Watch <code>active_energy</code> is an estimate, not a metabolic-cart
      measurement. Published validation studies suggest absolute accuracy within
      roughly ±10–15% versus indirect calorimetry, with consistency improving for
      cardiovascular activity over strength work. Use these numbers as a credible
      relative comparison between segments of one race rather than as a precise
      absolute burn figure.
    </p>
  </div>

</div>
</body>
</html>